Object.hasOwnProperty.call(obj, "a");

({}).hasOwnProperty.call(obj, "a");

const hasProperty = Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(object, property);
```

:::

Examples of **correct** code for this rule:

::: correct

```js
/*eslint prefer-object-has-own: "error"*/

